    {
      "__comment": "The barrel, running out through the chuck and most of the way across the empty block in front -- a Deployer's pole is modelled past its own boundary for the same reason. At rest the cutting head stops one pixel short of the block being printed into, and the helical travel is what closes that pixel, so the machine visibly bites what it is working on once a turn.",
